        "summary":  "Anthropic launched the Life Sciences Verification Program, granting researchers access to advanced models with tailored safeguards for biology work, including Standard Use grants for general research and High-risk Use grants for sensitive projects. The program reflects Anthropic\u0027s approach of domain-specific access tiers rather than universal model policies.",
        "execSummary":  "Anthropic is building tiered access frameworks for high-stakes domains — a model enterprise AI governance leaders should study as a template for internal AI policy. The distinction between Standard and High-risk Use tiers with differentiated monitoring shows that responsible AI deployment is increasingly domain-contextual, not one-size-fits-all. For enterprise leaders in regulated industries, this signals that AI providers are investing in sector-specific risk architectures, which could accelerate compliance approval for AI tooling. Key implication: enterprises should assess whether their AI vendor offers domain-appropriate safeguard tiers before broad deployment in sensitive workflows.",
