        "summary":  "AWS unveiled 13 new inference capabilities across Amazon SageMaker\u0027s managed endpoints and HyperPod Inference in 2026, addressing deployment efficiency, latency optimization, and operational observability. Key features include container caching that reduces startup time by 51% and prefix-aware routing that cuts time-to-first-token by up to 77% for long-context workloads.",
        "execSummary":  "AWS SageMaker\u0027s 13 inference upgrades in a single year reflect the intensifying competition to own enterprise AI infrastructure — and the 77% latency improvement for long-context workloads is a material operational advantage for enterprises running large document or conversation-based AI at scale. For enterprise AI platform owners, this is a concrete signal to re-benchmark SageMaker against current workloads, particularly if latency or cold-start time has been a barrier to production adoption. The container caching feature also reduces per-request cost, improving TCO for high-volume deployments. Caveat: AWS infrastructure lock-in is real — evaluate portability requirements before deep SageMaker integration.",
