        "execSummary":  "NVIDIA\u0027s new Vera Rubin NVL72 platform is setting new inference performance records — a signal that the gap between leading and lagging AI infrastructure is widening. For enterprise leaders, this matters because inference cost is the primary lever controlling the economics of production AI deployments; higher tokens-per-second at scale directly lowers cost-per-query. The 3.7x throughput gain is NVIDIA-reported and should be validated against your own workload mix before capital decisions, but the directionality is clear. Organizations running high-volume AI workloads — including customer-support automation — should pressure-test their infrastructure refresh cycles against this generation.",
