        "summary":  "Salesforce unveiled AIforce at Dreamforce 2026, an interface layer that connects its data, customer, and AI capabilities with external productivity platforms including Slack, Microsoft Teams, and ChatGPT, enabling organizations to build tailored UIs while maintaining data governance within the Salesforce ecosystem. CEO Marc Benioff framed it as a shift from workers going to Salesforce to Salesforce coming to workers across any tool they use.",
        "execSummary":  "AIforce represents Salesforce\u0027s strategic response to the threat of AI assistants and agents displacing traditional CRM interfaces — by embedding itself into whatever productivity tool employees already use. For enterprise and customer-support leaders already on the Salesforce platform, this is a significant architectural evolution worth evaluating: it could reduce context-switching friction for support agents and accelerate AI-assisted workflows. The critical caveats from analysts are real — AIforce adds cost on top of existing Salesforce licensing, and it only works well if the underlying CRM data is clean and well-governed. Treat this as a roadmap signal and begin data quality remediation now if AIforce is on your horizon.",
        "vendorLean":  "Neutral",
