        "date":  "2026-09-16",
        "theme":  "Strategy",
        "summary":  "Diverging safety philosophies among major AI vendors — with Meta pushing for independent model evaluators, Anthropic calling for a slower pace, and OpenAI advocating coordinated safety protocols — are creating tangible friction for enterprise IT organizations. The disagreements affect how enterprises procure, deploy, and govern AI systems.",
        "execSummary":  "The AI safety debate is no longer an academic argument — it is beginning to dictate which models enterprises can deploy and under what conditions. Vendor fragmentation on safety standards means procurement, legal, and IT teams face a moving compliance target with no single authoritative framework to anchor to. For support and operations leaders, this creates vendor-lock-in risk: a model approved today may face restrictions tomorrow if a vendor\u0027s safety posture shifts. The strategic play is to design AI deployments with modular model layers so that swapping vendors requires configuration changes, not full re-engineering.",
