        "title":  "Stop tuning your models and fix your data",
        "source":  "InfoWorld",
        "url":  "https://www.infoworld.com/article/4222975/stop-tuning-your-models-and-fix-your-data.html",
        "date":  "2026-09-17",
        "theme":  "Enterprise",
        "summary":  "A practitioner\u0027s account from Runpod\u0027s development of a conversational data agent found that switching to a more capable model produced only marginal quality improvements, while hardening the underlying data architecture fundamentally improved agent response usefulness. The author argues that enterprises racing to upgrade AI models are misallocating investment when their data foundations have missing joins, undocumented columns, and fragmented pipelines.",
        "execSummary":  "Before authorizing the next AI model upgrade, enterprise leaders should audit the data plumbing underneath it — because a smarter model on dirty data delivers wrong answers faster and more confidently, at scale. The Runpod case study is a concrete proof point: data architecture improvements outperformed model upgrades on quality metrics in a production agentic system. For customer-support AI specifically, this means CRM data hygiene, ticket taxonomy consistency, and knowledge-base completeness are higher-leverage investments than model version bumps. The key caveat: this argument applies most forcefully to task-specific enterprise agents; general-purpose model quality gaps still matter for open-domain queries.",
