        "summary":  "Wharton finance professor Jessica Wachter\u0027s analysis projects that AI infrastructure spending will reach nearly $1.1 trillion by 2027, requiring the investing companies to increase their own productivity by a factor of 2.7 by 2030 just to break even. The piece positions the current AI infrastructure boom as the highest-stakes capital allocation event in modern tech history.",
        "execSummary":  "The trillion-dollar AI infrastructure bet determines which AI services remain funded, competitive, and available for enterprise buyers over the next four years. Wachter\u0027s 2.7x productivity requirement is a sobering benchmark: if hyperscalers fall short, pricing pressure, service rationalization, or platform consolidation are likely outcomes that will directly affect enterprise AI roadmaps and vendor relationships. For leaders building multi-year AI strategies, this analysis argues for avoiding deep integration with platforms that cannot demonstrate a credible path to those returns. The implication for procurement is to pressure-test vendor financial stability alongside technical capability in every major AI platform evaluation.",
